From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:00:00 +0200
Subject: HID: sony: start the Sixaxis sticks centered

A DualShock 3 plugged in by USB sends no input report until its PS
button is pressed (sixaxis_set_operational_usb() and the deferred
initialization in sony_input_configured() say as much). Until then its
input device keeps the values the input core started it with, and every
axis starts at 0. The sticks are logical 0..255 with the rest position at
128, so 0 is both sticks pushed fully up and to the left: EVIOCGABS gives
0, joydev's initial JS_EVENT_INIT events give -32767, and SDL's evdev
joystick backend (which reads the axes with EVIOCGABS when a game opens
the pad) reports -32768 on both stick axes. Games take that as a held
stick. Seen with Quakespasm on SDL3: with an inactive DS3 on the cable,
the menu cursor runs up by itself until the PS button is pressed or the
pad is unplugged.

Set ABS_X, ABS_Y, ABS_RX and ABS_RY to the middle of their range in
input_configured, before the input device is registered, for the Sixaxis
and the Navigation controller (the same report). L2/R2 (ABS_Z, ABS_RZ)
rest at 0 and stay there. Once the pad reports, its real values replace
these as before.

Tested with a uhid DS3 (the hid-tools PS3Controller descriptor, 054c:0268
on BUS_USB) under QEMU: before any input report, EVIOCGABS shows 0 on
all four stick axes without the patch and 128 with it, and joydev's
initial axis events go from -32767 to 0; reports afterwards are reported
unchanged.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-sony.c b/drivers/hid/hid-sony.c
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-sony.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-sony.c
@@ -1878,6 +1878,29 @@ static inline void sony_cancel_work_sync(struct sony_sc *sc)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * A Sixaxis or Navigation controller on USB sends no input report until its
+ * PS button is pressed, and every axis starts at 0 in the input core. For the
+ * sticks (logical 0..255, centered at 128) 0 is fully up and to the left, and
+ * evdev, joydev and everything built on them report it as held for as long
+ * as the controller stays inactive. Start the sticks centered; the triggers
+ * (ABS_Z, ABS_RZ) rest at 0 already.
+ */
+static void sixaxis_center_sticks(struct input_dev *input)
+{
+	static const unsigned int sticks[] = { ABS_X, ABS_Y, ABS_RX, ABS_RY };
+	unsigned int i, code;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sticks); i++) {
+		code = sticks[i];
+		if (!test_bit(code, input->absbit))
+			continue;
+		input_abs_set_val(input, code,
+				  (input_abs_get_min(input, code) +
+				   input_abs_get_max(input, code) + 1) / 2);
+	}
+}
+
 static void sony_cleanup(struct sony_sc *sc)
 {
 	sony_cancel_work_sync(sc);
@@ -2014,6 +2037,9 @@ static int sony_input_configured(struct hid_device *hdev,
 		sony_init_output_report(sc, motion_send_output_report);
 	}
 
+	if (sc->quirks & (SIXAXIS_CONTROLLER | NAVIGATION_CONTROLLER))
+		sixaxis_center_sticks(hidinput->input);
+
 	if (sc->quirks & SONY_LED_SUPPORT) {
 		ret = sony_leds_init(sc);
 		if (ret < 0)
